abstract: >-
  Reproducible R pipeline (metafor, mada) for a systematic review and meta-analysis of cerebrospinal fluid
  (CSF) biomarkers in idiopathic normal pressure hydrocephalus (iNPH) compared with healthy controls and
  Alzheimer's disease. It pools standardized mean differences with random-effects models and prediction
  intervals, pools diagnostic sensitivity and specificity (bivariate or univariate models), and runs the
  leave-one-out, sensitivity, subgroup, age meta-regression and small-study analyses, rendering all
  supplementary figures and tables. The extracted study-level data are included.
keywords:
  - idiopathic normal pressure hydrocephalus
  - cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - meta-analysis
  - diagnostic test accuracy
  - R
